From e4a0bde68cd229f7f9e473e4c8d5d1cc092b6d08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:59:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] fix(render): retain styles incrementally when shadow
 roots carry stylesheets

Any document with a native shadow root switched the retained-style path
off, so every geometry read after a DOM change re-cascaded the whole
document (nytimes.com logs `retained-style fallback reason=shadow-sheets
roots=22`; 1.5-2 s per cascade). With container queries the second query
pass was a full cascade too, so each read cost two.

Shadow scopes:
- StylesheetCache keeps one compiled sheet per ShadowRoot; the root's
  ordered <style> text, viewport and media type are its fingerprint. A new
  root or a changed fingerprint restyles that host's component. Identical
  component sheets are parsed once per render.
- The planner walks the style tree (shadow children, slot -> assigned
  nodes) for subtrees and ancestor chains, and looks up the sheets that can
  select a node: its scope, its own shadow sheet (:host), and the scopes
  it is slotted into (::slotted). Slot reassignment (`slot`, slot `name`,
  slots entering or leaving a shadow tree) restyles the host's component.
- `:host(<compound>)` arguments are now keyed in the invalidation map, and
  `::slotted(<compound>)` is keyed as its own subject.
- Shadow <style> edits no longer force a full cascade; document-scope ones
  still do.
- Elements with no retained style are marked fresh so post-cascade
  normalization runs on them.
- obscura-js reports mutations inside shadow trees and attachShadow on a
  connected host to the retained planner instead of dropping the prepared
  render.

Container-query passes after the first re-cascade only the elements some
conditional rule selects (plus subtrees and ancestor chains) and reuse the
rest; full passes remain when a shadow sheet has conditional rules.

Tests: equivalence with a full cascade for shadow attribute/insert/remove/
text, shadow-root appends that bring slots, slotted children, host
attributes and inline style, slot reassignment, shadow <style> text and
insertion, and attachShadow after layout; locality (a mutation in one of 30
components re-cascades <= 40 nodes, 2000+ reused); container passes against
forced full passes, including a 5-level activation chain.

